			"Message": "feat(Output): Add localGit routing and Batch 6 IPC channel stubs\n\nAdd the `localGit` channel route mapping to route VS Code's built-in Git extension IPC to Mountain's `git:*` subprocess handlers. This fixes the SourceControl panel hanging forever at load with `InvokeMountain(\"undefined:exec\")`.\n\nAdd Batch 6 medium-priority channel stubs for services stock VS Code exposes via the shared process that Land doesn't implement: test results storage, profile storage listener, checksum service, language packs, user data sync utilities/machines/resource provider, custom endpoint telemetry, tunnel services, web content extraction, playwright automation, and V8 profiling.\n\nAlso enhance `InvokeMountain` with per-invoke timing telemetry logged to the `tauri-invoke` tag, capturing round-trip duration including Tauri transport overhead. This differentiates slow Rust handlers (large `ipc done t_ns`) from starved webview channels (large `tauri-invoke elapsed_ms` but small Rust-side time).",
			"SHA": "a79767ad78cd9de37302e3fddb58e95cffd93e79"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2026-04-23T16:55:03Z",
			"File": [
				"⠁⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				218,
				3
			],
			"Message": "perf(Output): Add telemetryAppender and mcpGalleryManifest stubs\n\nAdd two IPC channel stubs to eliminate the last remaining Tauri round-trips per session. The `telemetryAppender` stub (log/flush methods) removes 155 unnecessary IPC calls observed per boot in `channel-stub` output - by far the hottest miss. The `mcpGalleryManifest` stub removes the sole remaining `miss` per session for MCP gallery bootstrap.\n\nAlso fix _DevLogForward to send BOTH casings (Tag/Message + tag/message) to handle Tauri's param-case handling, with fallback to __TAURI_INTERNALS__.invoke for better compatibility.\n\nThese stubs short-circuit in the TS layer instead of crossing to Rust, improving renderer startup performance.",
			"SHA": "d6c52e8824c430206d714a117284cadb5355159d"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2026-04-23T15:57:08Z",
			"File": [
				"⠁⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				218,
				3
			],
			"Message": "feat(Output): Add DevLogForward to mirror IPC channel traffic to Mountain\n\nAdd a _DevLogForward helper function to TauriMainProcessService that mirrors IPC channel routing decisions into Mountain's dev-log file sink. This enables developers to trace TS-originated IPC traffic alongside Rust dev_log! output using LAND_DEV_LOG=channel-stub tail -f Mountain.dev.log.\n\nThe helper is invoked in three code paths: fire-and-forget channels (logger, output), stub hits (channel has a handler), and misses (no route, no stub). Each invocation logs the channel name, command, route prefix, and hit/miss status.\n\nThis is a fire-and-forget mechanism that never awaits or throws, matching the existing _Trace helper. It's a mirror of the helper already present in Wind's TauriMainProcessService.",
			"SHA": "618100a9bddfce70247a0abee72adcbc42a5e133"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2026-04-23T15:33:12Z",
			"File": [
				"⠁⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				218,
				3
			],
			"Message": "fix(Output): Add missing diagnostics stub methods\n\nAdd `getWorkspaceFileExtensions` and fix `reportWorkspaceStats` stub shapes in TauriMainProcessService diagnostics channel.\n\nThe `languageDetectionWorker ServiceImpl.resolveWorkspaceLanguageIds` iterates `fileExtensions.extensions` directly and throws without this stub, causing renderer crashes when language detection runs. Also fixes `reportWorkspaceStats` from `undefined` to a proper object shape with configFiles, fileTypes, and launchConfigFiles arrays.\n\nThis ensures the diagnostics IPC channel returns valid shapes that VS Code's services expect.",
			"SHA": "8131d76472e855192ba38169571d6c956eddc6b4"
		},
